  "method_notes": [
    "Warm synthetic local measurements on the same isolated 2 CPU / 2 GiB ClickHouse server.",
    "Exactly the same two million retained inference facts as baseline f60ed15e; source copied server-side, no production data.",
    "Baseline uses three repetitions, candidate five. Costs are totals in reports/query_costs and normalized per repetition in comparison.",
    "The new section returns totals, time series, task/model/effort breakdowns and approximate p50/p95; the old report contract differs.",
    "Initial raw+canonical ingestion uses 91 bounded source primary-key ranges, per-query memory 256 MiB; no Python two-million-row JSON transfer.",
    "Production bootstrap uses real RollupPublisher.refresh_one batch32 plus fenced PostgreSQL acknowledgements and 12 atomic compactions.",
    "The fixture injects all initial dirty keys with one bounded UNNEST call. Service-loop sleeps and full PG-to-CH export are not included in measured bootstrap work.",
    "Larger all-history and seven-day fixture aggregation attempts hit the 256 MiB cap. The successful production builder uses at most 32 hourly cohorts; daily coverage uses one day.",
    "PostgreSQL trials use a fresh isolated database, eight alternating rolled-back trials. New trigger overhead must be compared within each control population; old/new absolute trigger timings are not paired.",
    "Separate 16-shard audience gauge fixture: 32 synthetic account/feed observations, three alternating rounds, durable async acknowledgements unchanged; 2.170897s sequential versus0.140220s batched median (15.482x),16 queries/32 inserts versus1 query/2 inserts. This does not measure historical report latency."
